scope_hero_vs_secondary:
HERO: Share-to-check plus link-out (marketplace integration), built on a minimal Skin Profile, which every flow needs. SUPPORTING (light): Skin Forecast and Aisle Check, both reusing the hero's rules engine and result card. Plan for about 14h:

- H0-1, de-risk on a real phone before writing features:
  - share one product from the Amazon.in app and one from the Flipkart app into a notes app and log the payload;
  - tap the Flipkart facet URL and the Amazon /s?k= URL to see whether they open in-app;
  - get the YouCam key, deploy the Worker proxy, run one Skin Analysis call, and record the actual skin_type enum values and response shape.
- H1-4, Skin Profile:
  - consent screen, guided capture, upload and poll through the proxy, Skin Analysis SD subset plus Facial Color Tones;
  - band display, fairness note, local storage, photo deletion, 'What we keep' screen.
- H4-7.5, HERO:
  - expo-share-intent with an EAS dev build (start the build early, in parallel);
  - parser and editable title, seed catalogue (25-40 products, INCI from brand sites with a source URL per row) and a CosIng-cited actives table of about 30 rows;
  - deterministic rules, result card, link builders for Flipkart facet, Amazon.in keyword and Nykaa keyword;
  - 'Back to product' button.
- H7.5-9, Skin Forecast: Open-Meteo card, about 8 rules, a city picker with hard-coded coordinates for about 20 Indian cities, a travel-kit checklist, and the UV signal feeding the hero rules.
- H9-11, Aisle Check:
  - barcode scan with catalogue lookup, then Open Beauty Facts with a proper User-Agent, then UNKNOWN; reuses the result card;
  - referral checklist;
  - pharmacist QR backed by Worker KV with a 30-minute TTL, a revoke button, and a plain web view of the bands.
- H11-12, STRETCH only if on schedule: App Links for /p and /l on our domain (assetlinks.json plus SHA256), and a shareable skin-matched list.
- H12-14:
  - copy pass for guardrails (cosmetic wording, referral, credits 'Data: Open Beauty Facts (ODbL)' and 'Weather: Open-Meteo (CC BY 4.0)');
  - README with a 'What's possible / not possible' section, APK release, and recording the demo video.
- Cut list if behind, in order: App Links stretch, travel kit (keep the single weather card), Nykaa link, Open Beauty Facts lookup (catalogue only).
Never cut: consent, photo deletion, the referral line, the hero share-in, and the Flipkart filtered link-out.
